      "markdown": "## Sliding Window Maximum\n\nGiven `nums = [1, 3, -1, -3, 5, 3, 6, 7]` and a window size $k = 3$, report the maximum of every contiguous window: `[3, 3, 5, 5, 6, 7]`.\n\nA {{glossary:sliding window}} moves one position at a time. Re-scanning each window costs $O(k)$, so the naive answer is $O(nk)$.\n\nOpen the **Knowledge Graph** section below to see how this problem connects to the data structure that solves it in $O(n)$.",
